# The number data of CLDR release 49 for every locale it holds, which
# `i18n/numbers` reads: each locale's numbering systems, and for each system
# its symbols, its patterns and its compact patterns, as indices into the
# tables below; each locale's currency symbols; the ten digits of every
# numbering system that has them; the digits of the currencies whose amounts
# are not written with two; the currency each region uses today.
#
# A block's fields are separated by U+0001 and a list's entries by U+0002.
#
# Generated, never edited by hand: the Heroes program `generators/i18n_numbers/`
# read CLDR 49's JSON, `cldr-49.0.0-json-full.zip` of
# https://github.com/unicode-org/cldr-json/releases/download/49.0.0/
# (SHA-256
# 3b1f5d684d29c541d3acf91fe834b3fe36ae0f34775e3ee50e93558bf14ca174,
# fetched 2026-11-21), its files `cldr-numbers-full/main/*/numbers.json` and
# `currencies.json`, and `cldr-core`'s `availableLocales.json`,
# `supplemental/numberingSystems.json` and `currencyData.json`, and wrote this
# module whole; its `check` command says whether this module is still what
# it writes.

# The locales, `und` the root, in the order of their bytes.
